## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-conscious OTCA design, multi-tenant residency, and deletion rights in a real-world, cross-region telemetry pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- PII redaction and tokenization at ingress
- Tenant opt-in/out governance and regional routing
- Immutable audit logs for compliance
- Deletion requests via tombstones with cross-region propagation
- End-to-end testing including opt-out, deletion, and reconciliation

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPII(event) {
  const e = {...event};
  if (e.payload?.email) e.payload.email = 'REDACTED';
  if (e.payload?.phone) e.payload.phone = 'REDACTED';
  return e;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate no PII leaks in dashboards across regions?
- What metrics would you monitor to detect deletion propagation delays?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to enforce data quality at ingestion in a beginner OTCA setting, with per-tenant controls and end-to-end lifecycle.

## Key Concepts

- Ingest-time validation and whitelist
- Idempotency and dedup
- Per-tenant partitioning in storage
- Auditability of dropped records

## Code Example

```javascript
function validate(event, knownTenants){
  if(!event.tenant_id || !knownTenants.includes(event.tenant_id)) return false;
  if(!['login','click','error','latency'].includes(event.event_type)) return false;
  const ts = new Date(event.timestamp);
  const now = new Date();
  if(isNaN(ts) || Math.abs(now - ts) > 7*24*60*60*1000) return false;
  if(event.latency_ms != null && event.latency_ms < 0) return false;
  return true;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema evolution at ingestion without breaking existing pipelines?
- How would you implement a lightweight audit log for dropped events and partial successes?
